  <h1>Contract Edge Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Effective date: November 15, 2026</p>

  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Contract Edge handles information
    when you use the Contract Edge mobile application.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contract Edge is a manual-entry probability and expected-value
    calculator designed to help users evaluate binary event contracts.
    The application is designed to operate locally on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    Contract Edge does not require an account or registration.
    The application does not intentionally collect or transmit
    calculator inputs or personal information to the developer.
  </p>
  <p>
    The audited release does not include advertising or third-party
    analytics integrations.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information You Enter</h2>
  <p>
    You may manually enter contract prices, probability estimates,
    fees, quantities, and other values needed for calculations.
    These inputs are processed locally by the application.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contract Edge does not intentionally maintain a user profile
    or transaction history.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Internet and Network Access</h2>
  <p>
    Contract Edge is designed to operate offline. The Android
    application does not request the Android Internet permission,
    and its WebView is configured to block network loads.
  </p>
  <p>
    The application does not connect to prediction-market exchanges,
    brokerage accounts, or financial accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Local Storage</h2>
  <p>
    The application may use local caching to support offline access
    to application resources. This information is stored locally
    on the device.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    The audited release does not integrate advertising networks,
    analytics services, or prediction-market trading services.
    Third-party distribution platforms may process information
    under their own privacy policies and terms.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Contract Edge does not require users to submit personal
    information to use its calculator features. The application
    is not designed to collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Contract Edge is designed to minimize information handling
    by processing calculator inputs locally and restricting
    network access within the application. No method of storing
    or processing information can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy may be updated when application functionality
    or privacy practices change. Updated versions will be published
    on this page with a revised effective date.
  </p>

